Manage training jobs

Usage
  azd ai training job [command]

Available Commands
  cancel        : Cancel a running training job
  connect-ssh   : Open an SSH session to a node of a running training job
  delete        : Delete a training job
  download      : Download outputs and/or artifacts from a training job
  list          : List all training jobs
  show          : Show details of a specific training job
  show-services : Show services of a training job per node (e.g. SSH, JupyterLab, TensorBoard)
  stream        : Stream logs from a running training job
  submit        : Submit a new training job from a YAML definition file
  validate      : Validate a job YAML definition file offline without submitting

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string              : Sets the current working directory
      --debug                   : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string      : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help                    : help for job
      --no-prompt               : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string           : The output format (default "default")
      --project-endpoint string : Azure AI Foundry project endpoint URL (e.g., https://account.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/project-name)
  -s, --subscription string     : Azure subscription ID (enables implicit init if environment not configured)

Examples
  Validate a job definition before submitting it
    azd ai training job validate --file job.yaml
    azd ai training job submit --file job.yaml

Use azd ai training job [command] --help to view examples and more information about a specific command.
